            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for a snake, then the Bengali for a crow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ভালুক",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ভালুক — bhāluk — \"a bear\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ভালুক (bhāluk) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from bhallukka, \"bear\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 9415). It stands beside Sanskrit bhallūka, \"bear\", whose source is disputed: CDIAL reports both an Indo-European origin and Przyluski's Austroasiatic one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
